ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":100,"prev":102,"next":105,"titles":108,"firmware":25},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":26,"procedures":56,"parameters":57,"related":83,"body":86,"sources":87,"official_url":30,"controls":95},"fx.delay","Delay effect",[5,6,7,8,9],"delay","echo","delay fx","delay time","repeats","fx",20,"knowledge/manual/units/fx/delay.md",{"modes":14,"screens":16},[15],"auxiliary",[17],"M1","An echo for FX I or FX II; `M1` sets the repeat spacing as a note value, fine-tunes it, and sets the feedback and the amount of dry signal.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[23],"1.1.25","1.1.15","1.1.33",[27,33,38,41,44,48,52],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"what","The delay plays back what it receives as a series of echoes.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/fx#delay",null,"official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":36,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":37},"size","Size (`E1`) sets the spacing of the repeats and reads as a note value, such as 1/8 dotted.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#213-auxiliary-tracks","verified",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":36,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":37},"labels","The delay's columns read size, fine, feedback and dry — `E2` fine-tunes the spacing and `E3` sets the feedback.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"dry","Dry (`E4`) sets the untreated signal against the echoes; at 0 only the repeats are heard.",{"id":45,"text":46,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":47},"dry-ends","A new project keeps dry at 99, where each sending track keeps its own sound and the echoes come on top, as a send. Turned down, more of what a track sends is heard only through the delay, and at 0 a track sending at 99 is heard as repeats alone. The replica plays it this way; how the unit mixes in between is not yet measured.","derived",{"id":9,"text":49,"source":50,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":51},"The repeats sit in the centre of the stereo field, not bouncing left and right, and keep their bass; each repeat is about 4.4 dB quieter than the one before at feedback 50 (one video, measured at 95 BPM, OS 1.1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":55,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"jitter","Since OS 1.1.25 the delay stays steady when the tempo of an external clock wobbles.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",[],[58,66,72,78],{"screen":17,"encoder":59,"layer":60,"keys":61,"name":34,"range":62,"default":31,"cc":63,"cc_confidence":64,"note":65,"source":36,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":37},"E1","base","turn E1","note values, e.g. 1/8 dotted",12,"community-verified","coarse spacing between repeats",{"screen":17,"encoder":67,"layer":60,"keys":68,"name":69,"range":31,"default":31,"cc":70,"cc_confidence":64,"note":71,"source":36,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":37},"E2","turn E2","fine",13,"fine-tunes the spacing; the guide calls it amount",{"screen":17,"encoder":73,"layer":60,"keys":74,"name":75,"range":31,"default":31,"cc":76,"cc_confidence":64,"note":77,"source":36,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":25,"confidence":37},"E3","turn E3","feedback",14,"how many repeats come back; the guide calls it fine",{"screen":17,"encoder":79,"layer":60,"keys":80,"name":42,"range":31,"default":31,"cc":81,"cc_confidence":64,"note":82,"source":30,"firmware_min":31,"verified_on":31,"confidence":32},"E4","turn E4",15,"level of the untreated signal",[84,85],"fx.overview","fx.reverb","Set the rough echo distance with size, then fine-tune it and choose how long the echoes keep coming\nback. Dry at 99, as a new project has it, is the classic send; at 0 the echoes replace the sound.\nTE's guide calls the\nmiddle controls amount and fine and describes size as eight named steps from micro to insane; on\n1.1.33 the screen reads fine and feedback, and size shows note values, so the spacing follows the\ntempo.",[88,90,92,93],{"url":30,"kind":89},"guide",{"url":36,"kind":91},"research",{"url":50,"kind":91},{"url":55,"kind":94},"changelog",[96,97,98,99],"encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":10,"title":101},"Effects",{"id":103,"title":104},"fx.chorus","Chorus effect",{"id":106,"title":107},"fx.distortion","Distortion effect",{"basics.key-notation":109,"basics.main-modes":110,"basics.modules":111,"basics.track-buttons":112,"basics.linked-tracks":113,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":114,"basics.workflow":115,"basics.firmware-versions":116,"hardware.layout":117,"hardware.power-and-charging":118,"hardware.connectors":119,"hardware.specifications":120,"hardware.te-boot":121,"hardware.firmware-update":122,"hardware.factory-reset":123,"hardware.system-menu":124,"hardware.safety-and-care":125,"hardware.in-the-box":126,"sequencer.overview":127,"sequencer.step-entry":128,"sequencer.step-recording":129,"sequencer.live-recording":130,"sequencer.extend-notes":131,"sequencer.nudge":132,"sequencer.single-sound":133,"sequencer.rotate":134,"sequencer.copy-step":135,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":136,"sequencer.parameter-locks":137,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":138,"sequencer.step-components":139,"sequencer.step-component-reference":140,"sequencer.component-pulse":141,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":142,"sequencer.component-multiply":143,"sequencer.component-velocity":144,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":145,"sequencer.component-ramp-down":146,"sequencer.component-random":147,"sequencer.component-portamento":148,"sequencer.component-bend":149,"sequencer.component-tonality":150,"sequencer.component-jump":151,"sequencer.component-skip-parameter-lock":152,"sequencer.component-skip-step-component":153,"sequencer.component-skip-trigger":154,"sequencer.bar-menu":155,"sequencer.track-scale":156,"sequence